{{Quote|My world tried to avoid taking sides in the war, but the Separatists staged a coup in the guise of ''legitimate political'' action.|Saw Gerrera|<ref name="MOF">''[[Reign of the Empire: The Mask of Fear]]''</ref>}}
In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Date note" /> at the [[First Battle of Geonosis|start]] of the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" /> the Confederacy '''invaded''' the [[Planet|world]] of [[Onderon]] in the [[Inner Rim Territories]]<ref name="BTCTG" /> after staging<ref name="MOF" /> and covertly supporting a pro-Separatist coup. Legally speaking, the [[Confederacy military]] was "invited" to Onderon by [[Sanjay Rash]], a Separatist puppet who came to power through the coup.<ref name="TCW">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Clone Wars}}</ref> In reality, however, the incident was an invasion, with Rash even having been appointed by [[Count]] [[Dooku]].<ref name="BTCTG" />

==The invasion==
{{Quote|Onderon is in your king's rule, and at the outbreak of the Clone War, he chose to align it with the Separatists.''"<br />"''Our true king has been ''silenced''. The one you recognize is a ''traitor'' and a Separatist minion.|[[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Saw Gerrera]]|<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" />}}
During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Onderonian]] [[king]], [[Ramsis Dendup]], had refused to side with either the [[Galactic Republic]] nor [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] due to the corruption in both<ref name="DB Ramsis">{{Databank|king-ramsis-dendup|King Ramsis Dendup}}</ref> and hoped a neutral stance would spare [[Onderon]] from the damages of the fighting.<ref name="Sanjay Rash Databank">{{Databank|king-sanjay-rash|King Sanjay Rash}}</ref> With some under his rule deeming him a coward but seeing the moment as a chance to grab power, [[Sanjay Rash]], who deemed an alliance with the Separatists the best way to ensure Onderon's future, managed to become the new king through unclear means.<ref name="DB Ramsis" /> The Confederacy covertly supported a coup that brought him to power.<ref name="TCW" />

Rash was appointed to the position of king by [[Count]] [[Dooku]] to serve as a Separatist puppet.<ref name="BTCTG" /> Legally speaking, however, the planet withdrew from the Republic on Rash's order. The Droid Army was "invited" to Onderon to help with security,<ref name="TCW" /> but the action was truly an invasion.<ref name="BTCTG" /> Nevertheless, any open response from Republic would be branded an act of aggression thanks to Rash's legal standing<ref name="TCW" /> and Onderon's history of neutrality.<ref name="Dawn Rebels">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> However, the invasion and Rash's appointment inspired a [[Onderon rebels|resistance movement]]<ref name="BTCTG" /> that began the [[Onderonian Civil War]].<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" />

[[Journalist]] [[Ricta Varsh]] of [[HoloNet News]] reported from Onderon during the coup.<ref name="GT:AitC">{{InsiderCite|237|Galactic Tales: Another Face in the Crowd}}</ref>

